ved `--dht-*` flags with `--index-store mem`), refuse\n    94\t  startup, naming the file and `--reset`. A state file that cannot be written\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn resolve-flags\n   105\t  \"The flags this run starts with: `saved` overridden by `explicit`.  The\n   106\t   `unset` flags a subcommand clears (`dht serve` is never publishing and\n   107\t   holds no key, whatever was saved) are dropped from `saved` only, so a\n   108\t   flag the command line names explicitly always stands.\"\n   109\t  [saved explicit unset]\n   110\t  (merge (apply dissoc saved unset) explicit))\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(defn changed\n   441\t           true (into (mapcat #(vector \"--dht-peer\" %)) peers)\n   442\t           true (into rest))\n   443\t         {:new-key (when (= \"init\" verb) key)\n   444\t          :name name\n   445\t          :dir (or dir (state-path name \"\"))\n   446\t          ;; only `init` publishes and signs: a saved --dht-publish or\n   447\t          ;; --dht-key must not survive `serve` or `join` (a --key named on\n   448\t          ;; that command line still stands)\n   449\t          :unset (when-not (= \"init\" verb) #{\"--dht-publish\" \"--dht-key\"})}]))))\n   450\t\n### 5.8 Command line and saved state (decision 8)\n\n- **The token** is `yin:<host:port>/<principal>`, printed once when both\n  the socket and the board endpoint are bound. A token with a third part\n  is refused: a manifest is a pin and belongs to `--dht-manifest`.\n- **`dht join <token>`** becomes `--index-store dht:<dir> --dht-peer\n  <host:port> --dht-principal <hex> --dht-follow <hex>@<host:port>`. It\n  passes no `--dht-manifest`: its first manifest is the first trace it\n  installs. The shell admits evaluation at once and says, per followed\n  principal, whether a head is installed.\n- **`state.edn`** keeps flags, and gains `--dht-follow` (repeatable).\n  It never holds a head. `--dht-manifest` stays one-shot.\n- **Hydration is not removed and `--dht-recover` is not added.** The\n  defect was joining by hydration (D1), and join no longer does. What\n            saved {\"--dht-publish\" true \"--dht-key\" \"~/.yin/a.key\"\n                   \"--dht-peer\" [\"127.0.0.1:4002\"]}\n            resolve (fn [& args]\n                      (let [[args' extra] (repl/expand-args args)]\n                        (state/resolve-flags saved\n                                             (:flags (state/split-args args'))\n                                             (:unset extra))))]\n        (is (not (contains? (resolve \"dht\" \"serve\" \"--dir\" dir\n                                     \"--peer\" \"localhost:4002\")\n                            \"--dht-key\")))\n        (is (not (contains? (resolve \"dht\" \"join\" token \"--dir\" dir)\n                            \"--dht-key\")))\n        (is (= \"k2\" (get (resolve \"dht\" \"serve\" \"--dir\" dir \"--key\" \"k2\"\n                                  \"--peer\" \"localhost:4002\")\n                         \"--dht-key\"))\n            \"an explicit --key on serve is not dropped\")\n        (is (= \"k3\" (get (resolve \"dht\" \"init\" \"--dir\" dir \"--key\" \"k3\"\n                                  \"--peer\" \"localhost:4002\")\n                         \"--dht-key\"))\n            \"init keeps the key it is given\")))))\n\n\n(deftest dht-join-saves-its-follow-and-a-bare-start-resumes-it\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
